"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrispbsmolen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-10T05:06:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T05:06:57Z","body":"Hi Arhan, thank you for the CSV and for the ten pull requests. I checked your CSV against the table as it stands today. Of its 60 lines, the 28 at 2 and 3 symbols now give no value, which is what the new rule is for. Six lines at 20 to 25 symbols are now below your figures, because the Shokri, Moura and Stevens rows came in after you made the file (57,701 against your 58,230 at 20 symbols). The other 26 still stand above a rule I do not count yet, by 2 to 21 percent, the largest being 3029 against 2492 at 6 symbols from 10,001 to 10,610 columns. That is stated in section 6 of the conventions and it closes as I check each rule.\n\nI compared every strength-2 row with derived.csv by hand, as I said I would, and also with every product of two table sizes. At its own width or wider no row is beaten. Your rows win by 6 to 23 rows and the binary ones are the optimum. At narrower widths four of them stand above a product of two table rows. These are 369 at 9 symbols (349 up to 21,582 columns), 561 at 11 symbols (460 up to 20,460), 2047 at 23 symbols (1789 up to 20,136) and 2425 at 25 symbols (1949 up to 20,280), and the gap ends at 25,740, 47,740, 28,928 and 36,176 columns. You say this yourself in #72. I will merge them with that known. One more thing I noticed. With the extra column of the projective plane the same sizes reach further, for example 1105 up to 103,173 columns at 17 symbols and 637 up to 37,349 at 13. If you want to send those, they are welcome. I am merging in steps, smallest first, and will write here if anything looks different on main.\n\n-Christopher","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/comments/6759527172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/comments/6759603577","html_url":"https://github.com/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/62#issuecomment-6759603577","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/62","id":6759603577,"node_id":"IC_kwDOTsvulc8AAAABkuddeQ","user":{"login":"arhancanli","id":315329124,"node_id":"U_kgDOEsuKZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/315329124?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli","html_url":"https://github.com/arhancanli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-10T05:12:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T05:12:27Z","body":"Thank you, Christopher, for checking all of it by hand. Merging smallest first is fine with us, and we will watch main as each one lands.\n\nYes, we would like to send the extensions with the extra column of the projective plane (for example 1105 at 17 symbols up to 100,000 columns and 637 at 13 symbols up to 37,349). We will prepare them as new submissions after these ten are in, with the same checks as before.\n\nArhan\n\nPrepared with the help of Claude, an AI system from Anthropic; I take responsibility for it.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/comments/6759603577/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/comments/6786414350","html_url":"https://github.com/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/62#issuecomment-6786414350","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/62","id":6786414350,"node_id":"IC_kwDOTsvulc8AAAABlIB3Dg","user":{"login":"arhancanli","id":315329124,"node_id":"U_kgDOEsuKZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/315329124?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli","html_url":"https://github.com/arhancanli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arhancanli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-11T03:46:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T03:46:40Z","body":"Hi Christopher, a heads-up before we send strength-4 rows past 10,000 columns, so you can say no before your CI spends\nanything. We have three covering perfect hash families of strength 4 found by our own search, each at 100,000 columns, made\nmostly of progression rows (Singer rows of GF(q^4) and affine rows a^j and (b^j, j)), with a few random rows. Above\n65,535 columns fastprog cannot take them, so your planner would use cphfcheck progression. With your unit costs and the\nfactor 2 the estimates are:\n\n| family | N | progression rows / other | your estimate (core-hours, x2) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CPHF(18; 100000, 25, 4) | 7,031,233 | 14 / 4 | 2.1 for the hashing, about 1.1 more for the shift tests |\n| CPHF(17; 100000, 23, 4) | 4,757,281 | 14 / 3 | 2.4 for the hashing, about 0.04 more for the shift tests |\n| CPHF(21; 100000, 17, 4) | 1,753,921 | 16 / 5 | 4.5 for the hashing, about 2.3 more for the shift tests |\n\nFor q = 16 and below our families of this kind do not reach 100,000 columns (too many sets fail in every progression\nrow), so we would not send those. Each family already passes two exact checks: our refinement checker (t4ref) and your cphfcheck progression,\nrun here. Our separately written cells checker is still running at this width, and each pull request will say\nhow far it has got. We would send one family per pull request, one at a\ntime, waiting for your certificate workflow to finish each one. Is that all right, or would you prefer another order\nor fewer?\n\nArhan\n\nPrepared with the help of Claude, an AI system from Anthropic; I take responsibility for it.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrispbsmolen/ca-tools/issues/comments/6786414350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]